    "Validation episode support was broad rather than dominated by one trade: 26 completed episodes and 31.67719708 percent top-positive-episode contribution."
  ],
  "material_learning": "A fixed OBV moving-average state was highly regime-dependent rather than a durable participation edge. Primary 2/24 was excellent in Design, including strong 2020-2021 timing and a smaller 2022 loss than buy-and-hold, but in Validation it captured only 41.022945 percent of passive upside while maximum drawdown rose 9.37063649 percentage points and Calmar fell to 31.794450 percent of buy-and-hold. The two frozen slower-average neighbors preserved more upside but still had worse Validation drawdown and only 52.632455 to 54.936537 percent of passive Calmar. The 2024 fold was the clearest failure: only 22.709848 percent upside capture with worse drawdown. This supports the adversarial prior that a dynamically selected portfolio's OBV success does not transfer to one immutable tuple.",
  "scientific_claim": "The exact daily base-volume OBV SMA 2/24 long-or-zero-yield-cash policy and its preregistered 2/18 and 2/30 rejection-only neighbors produced positive after-cost historical returns but failed frozen Validation drawdown, upside-capture, Calmar and annual breadth gates. None is a candidate, and the result does not authorize choosing the better neighbor, a different length, EMA, band, delay, price confirmation, rolling selector, portfolio ensemble or DRA interaction.",
